# Generated machine-readable results (unit tier JUnit XML, accessibility evidence JSON
# and its sha256 sidecar) are never committed.
#
# The DIRECTORY itself is committed - via the negation below and the placeholder
# .results/.gitignore - so that a CLEAN CHECKOUT already has somewhere for
# `--test-reporter-destination` and the evidence command to write, with no mkdir,
# no install step and no first-run failure (AC-30). See WS-12.
.results/*
!.results/.gitignore
